{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:25:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_55462cb4c6484827b9b7f5719aa858eb","id":"pg_3c7339f3604f52b0990aa5b834de4635","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/xiaomimimo-mimo-code-use-restrictions-md-6fbb1732232c-a5b834de4635.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_de32145045c0516cb41f4ae26ee3d2a0"],"title":"XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-Code/USE_RESTRICTIONS.md @ 6fbb1732232c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:25:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_55462cb4c6484827b9b7f5719aa858eb"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_15240c53919e0e0e430d8728137c74f3bb4b04d4d00c7b9e6367afeb3b26045a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states MiMoCode does not support the built-in macOS Terminal.app, recommending iTerm2 or the VS Code integrated terminal for rendering issues."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2045fffbe584c14a0c4ac8123f674e87a3459fafa70a169f661d9c3dd9d6b935"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Workflows are deterministic JavaScript scripts orchestrating multiple agents with fixed phases, bounded retries, and automatic parallelization; four built-ins ship (compose, deep-research, fact-check, research-experiment), and custom ones go in .mimocode/workflows/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_34fa756b8b6e3b0863234103e432abd8f028ea360aea448417665ba6410f991a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Cross-session memory uses SQLite FTS5 with files for project memory (MEMORY.md), session checkpoints, scratch notes, and per-task progress; memory is injected automatically on session resume."},{"claim_ids":["clm_50be779ee40350ac4133631be84aa6ba913f0ae16ea3b1330e2c856e01a743e2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Context management includes automatic checkpoints, context reconstruction near the window limit, budgeted injection with importance ranking, and a per-model adjustable compaction point via /context-limit or compaction.max_context."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5bb0176e60f170b8b00bd0321b586e5178b37b447c1a16a0a04da0642accec96"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"File access outside the project directory triggers an external_directory permission prompt by default; /tmp can be allowlisted in config, and --dangerously-skip-permissions injects an allow-all base while explicit deny rules still block."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5c2f70f436c9fa63d9e3ae3b9cffd3f99adca62b60755283838e435c8eaa79b1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: development uses bun (bun ci for frozen-lockfile install, bun run dev, bun turbo typecheck)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6d2f9dc8fdb177e096afa178b202d7954a4ec4e5e3d59326b53dd323c927ec90"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The research-experiment workflow appears to provide an evaluation-style loop (baseline, iterate, audit against metric gaming) for mechanically verifiable metrics, though no benchmark results for the agent itself appear in the evidence."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7f428ee8bfe61832784054a38a4c543e48f72ac63446599ec62c647e154d5a4d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Environment variables can disable builtin skills entirely, disable only office/media skills, or hide skills from TUI autocomplete while keeping them available to agents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_82691afaae0191369c8dd1789400850834a02aa9753aa0437663f423b5adc04e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Three primary agents exist: build (full permissions), plan (read-only analysis), and compose (specs-driven orchestration); Tab switches agents, and Compose is isolated once entered."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9ec3c9d8c154fe705756b3126d4cc1c602d52c637b48deb43ba3b143e9817255"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MiMoCode is built as a fork of OpenCode, retaining core capabilities (multiple providers, TUI, LSP, MCP, plugins) and adding memory, context management, subagents, goal loops, and dream/distill self-improvement."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a6020a5783bf3448215b073d5bff068ebc49ad23fd49d7a4445298d153c5b87b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MiMoCode is a terminal-native AI coding assistant that reads/writes code, runs commands, manages Git, and maintains persistent project memory across sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ad593f13fd32fd787e180bf3843be20f9fee51c21cd55ba0eda850dadaafbc0a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The primary agent can spawn subagents that share session context, run in parallel, and support lifecycle tracking, cancellation, and background execution."},{"claim_ids":["clm_aed6f2a21a33d1228adcbb99fc28a99428e395453071a4559c24e6db87d443a4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Voice input requires the sox dependency and is available to MiMo logged-in users; the ASR model mimo-v2.5-asr is only on MiMo's platform while voice control works via OpenRouter-compatible providers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b66d64704c64f6d5d8e8a603d2ce2e7ab446afa6ab568bc1001b6e1cd74888d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Install options include a curl one-liner for macOS/Linux, a PowerShell script for Windows, and npm install -g @mimo-ai/cli; the CLI is launched with the `mimo` command."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c6e1a3789e00d96753593140255b3969b9fe57f76e0218dc715db158caf2590c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Builtin skills are matched by exact name, localized alias, or BM25 relevance; high-confidence matches auto-load, and users can override builtins with same-name skills in project or personal skill directories."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d75a00647fb28292f69dfaa5a7934867c3dbd213e4b315e192ea0a2a7a8490a1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"First launch offers configuration via Xiaomi MiMo OAuth, Codex/ChatGPT OAuth, one-step import from Claude Code, catalog providers, or any custom OpenAI-compatible API."}],"claim_ids":["clm_15240c53919e0e0e430d8728137c74f3bb4b04d4d00c7b9e6367afeb3b26045a","clm_2045fffbe584c14a0c4ac8123f674e87a3459fafa70a169f661d9c3dd9d6b935","clm_34fa756b8b6e3b0863234103e432abd8f028ea360aea448417665ba6410f991a","clm_50be779ee40350ac4133631be84aa6ba913f0ae16ea3b1330e2c856e01a743e2","clm_5bb0176e60f170b8b00bd0321b586e5178b37b447c1a16a0a04da0642accec96","clm_5c2f70f436c9fa63d9e3ae3b9cffd3f99adca62b60755283838e435c8eaa79b1","clm_6d2f9dc8fdb177e096afa178b202d7954a4ec4e5e3d59326b53dd323c927ec90","clm_7f428ee8bfe61832784054a38a4c543e48f72ac63446599ec62c647e154d5a4d","clm_82691afaae0191369c8dd1789400850834a02aa9753aa0437663f423b5adc04e","clm_9ec3c9d8c154fe705756b3126d4cc1c602d52c637b48deb43ba3b143e9817255","clm_a6020a5783bf3448215b073d5bff068ebc49ad23fd49d7a4445298d153c5b87b","clm_ad593f13fd32fd787e180bf3843be20f9fee51c21cd55ba0eda850dadaafbc0a","clm_aed6f2a21a33d1228adcbb99fc28a99428e395453071a4559c24e6db87d443a4","clm_b66d64704c64f6d5d8e8a603d2ce2e7ab446afa6ab568bc1001b6e1cd74888d6","clm_c6e1a3789e00d96753593140255b3969b9fe57f76e0218dc715db158caf2590c","clm_d75a00647fb28292f69dfaa5a7934867c3dbd213e4b315e192ea0a2a7a8490a1"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:25:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_55462cb4c6484827b9b7f5719aa858eb","id":"pg_8c942ba77f945125bf63a4d3cf997137","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/xiaomimimo-mimo-code-readme-md-6fbb1732232c-a4d3cf997137.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_90482fc645e750f795208ff2bb5d75a2"],"title":"XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-Code/README.md @ 6fbb1732232c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:25:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_55462cb4c6484827b9b7f5719aa858eb"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2990f3cc22d78682a10f6967c7ffc961156bfc83574fed19cc0fb69812d369c9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"For GPT/Codex models, a smaller tool ABI (bash, apply_patch, view_image, exec) is exposed; exec composes host tools inside QuickJS while permissions and side effects remain under host control."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5f7e36ab93631df2b87a88ce376a949ffe84becb0522f1b166b26b0caff321cb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The GPT profile is enabled when the model ID contains 'gpt-' (excluding 'oss' and 'gpt-4') and hides overlapping read/write/edit/grep/glob tools; prompt routing and tool profiles use separate string rules not yet unified."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2990f3cc22d78682a10f6967c7ffc961156bfc83574fed19cc0fb69812d369c9","clm_5f7e36ab93631df2b87a88ce376a949ffe84becb0522f1b166b26b0caff321cb"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:25:17Z","created_by_operation":"op_55462cb4c6484827b9b7f5719aa858eb","id":"pg_a36ec0092726553fbacfac92cd92af64","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/xiaomimimo-mimo-code-docs-architecture-codex-microkernel-runtime-en-md-ac92cd92af64.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_6b019d2dcaa65e8b94675c5a2066b0e4"],"title":"XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-Code/docs/architecture/codex-microkernel-runtime.en.md @ 6fbb1732232c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:25:17Z","updated_by_operation":"op_55462cb4c6484827b9b7f5719aa858eb"}
